WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.493
Correlation connects indicators from different public sources to understand possible relationships.

00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:15.820
Domains, subdomains, DNS answers, certificates, internet addresses, providers, repositories, packages, websites, and organizations can be arranged in a timeline or relationship map.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.115
Every connection should describe its evidence.

00:00:19.115 --> 00:00:23.729
A domain resolved to an address on a date.

00:00:23.729 --> 00:00:28.343
A certificate covered a hostname during a validity period.

00:00:28.343 --> 00:00:32.518
A repository referenced a domain in a file.

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:37.572
These statements are stronger than a vague line suggesting ownership.

00:00:37.572 --> 00:00:39.988
Time prevents false relationships.

00:00:39.988 --> 00:00:46.800
An address can be reassigned, a certificate can expire, and a vendor can change.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.974
Place observations on a timeline before combining them.

00:00:50.974 --> 00:00:56.907
Two indicators observed years apart may not describe the same operational state.

00:00:56.907 --> 00:01:04.597
Ownership indicators include official statements, authoritative records, consistent branding, repository control, contractual confirmation, and internal inventory.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.574
Each has limitations.

00:01:06.574 --> 00:01:12.067
Hosting, naming similarity, or one shared provider rarely proves common control.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:17.560
Assign confidence based on source quality, independence, consistency, and remaining alternatives.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.295
Look for disconfirming evidence and shared-infrastructure explanations.

00:01:21.295 --> 00:01:27.228
Avoid false attribution, which can waste response effort and harm unrelated parties.

00:01:27.228 --> 00:01:32.720
A relationship map is an analytical aid, not proof by appearance.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:43.926
Keep source identifiers attached to nodes and edges, distinguish observed facts from judgments, and report uncertainty so reviewers can challenge or update the model.
